<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  VirtualDriver verification scenario 08_overtake / overtake_aborted_for_route_branch

  vd-func:FUNC-056 (overtake maneuver) / req-vd-ad:REQ-AD-024 acceptance ladder
  step c ("追い越し中に経路ホップの締切が来たら追い越しを打ち切って戻る" -
  the section 5-2 safety valve).

  ============================ REVISION HISTORY =============================
  v1 (discarded): tightened the route-budget MARGIN. The coordinating
  session verified this author's own algebraic proof that this can never
  work: the "required" guard formula is self-consistent by construction, so
  margin-tightening alone can never make the safety valve fire.

  v2 (discarded): kept the guard on the generous-margin side and instead
  made SlowLead accelerate mid-pass to a speed just under Ego's (19.9 vs
  20.0 m/s), banking on the residual gap-to-clear still being small enough,
  at the moment the OUT hop completed, that a near-zero delta_v would blow
  the remaining route budget before natural clearing. This required a
  large, carefully-tuned g0=100.0m and a razor-thin-by-construction timing
  window (~0.4s) for the acceleration event, which this author flagged
  CONFIDENCE: LOW.

  v3 (this version, 2026-08-04): the coordinating session fixed two things
  in the C++ implementation that changed which scenario design actually
  exercises the safety valve:
    1. The valve now opens on the SIGNAL threshold (ShouldSignalLaneChangeHop)
       instead of the ARM threshold (ShouldAttemptLaneChangeHop). Opening on
       the arm threshold left no distance for the legally-required
       indicator dwell, and v2's real measurement showed the return
       indicator lead was only 0.05s (a REQ-AD-023 step d violation).
    2. SIGNAL_BACK no longer skips its dwell or gap-acceptance wait when the
       deadline arrives - the return hop now ALWAYS requires "dwell
       complete AND gap accepted", no exceptions.
  Given fix 2, the coordinating session identified that the return hop's
  own gap-acceptance requirement (max(lane_change_gap_min_m(8.0),
  v_pass*lane_change_gap_headway_lead_s(1.2)) = max(8.0,24.0) = 24.0 m) is
  LARGER than the "cleared" threshold (g1+L_ego/2+L_lead/2 = 13.0 m) -
  meaning by the time Ego could actually return, it has ALREADY cleared
  SlowLead in the ordinary "pass and come back" case. The ONLY physical way
  to return with cleared_lead staying false for the whole run is for
  SlowLead itself to pull AHEAD of Ego (accelerating past Ego's own cruise
  speed), opening the original lane's gap from the front while Ego can
  never actually get ahead of it.

  This version therefore reverts to v1's SIMPLE parameters (g0=40.0m, same
  as overtake_slow_lead_on_two_lane_road - no special tuning needed) and
  makes SlowLead accelerate to 25.0 m/s (5.0 m/s FASTER than Ego's 20.0
  m/s cruise), fired well after Ego has entered PASS (t=8.0s - comfortably
  past the sibling scenario's measured pass@6.40s under the same g0=40
  setup, and past the coordinating session's "any time after t~=7s" advice).
  This is DELIBERATELY not timing-sensitive: whenever the acceleration
  fires (as long as it is after PASS begins and before Ego would have
  cleared SlowLead under the original delta_v=12.0), the outcome is the
  same - SlowLead pulls away forever, Ego can never clear it, the original
  lane opens up ahead of SlowLead, the return hop's gap-acceptance is
  satisfied, and the ONLY way PASS ever ends is the section 5-2 safety
  valve forcing SIGNAL_BACK. No fine-tuned deadline arithmetic is needed
  (per the coordinating session: "しきい値のチューニングが要らなくなる").
  ============================================================================

  MEASURED (2026-08-04, this author's own batch run against the rebuilt
  DLL, GIT REV v3.4.1-863-9488c193-dirty): signal_out@0.05 -> out@3.00
  (outbound lead 2.95s) -> pass@6.40 -> signal_back@31.75 (route_budget_m=
  199.14, right at the ~200m SIGNAL threshold = 140m ARM threshold + 60m
  for the mandatory indicator dwell) -> back@34.75 (inbound lead 3.00s) ->
  idle@38.15. Final route_lane: deviation_count=0, on_target_lane=true -
  the safety valve protected the route successfully. Full must-list
  results and an important open FINDING about telemetry.overtake.
  cleared_lead's behavior are in the companion .expectations.yaml file
  (search "FINDING" there) - this author's measurement shows that field
  tracks the current phase (true for signal_back/back, false for
  idle/pass) rather than a live re-check against the captured SlowLead
  pointer once Ego has left its lane, which this author flagged for the
  coordinating session to judge rather than working around silently.

  == distance-budget arithmetic (identical to overtake_slow_lead_on_two_
  lane_road - see that file's header comment for the full derivation) ==
    v_pass = 20.0 m/s, v_lead_initial = 8.0 m/s, g0 = 40.0 m, L_ego=L_lead=
    5.0 m, g1=8.0 m => L_clear=58.0 m, t_pass=4.8333s (<=overtake_max_
    pass_time_s=10.0 read from config/virtual_driver.json), required=
    496.667 m against dist_to_connection=770.0 m (Ego starts at road0 s=30,
    same as the sibling scenario) - guard passes with the same comfortable
    273.33 m margin.

  Acceleration event: SimulationTimeCondition value="8.0" steps SlowLead
  from 8.0 to 25.0 m/s. Once SlowLead is faster than Ego, the relative gap
  (Ego rear vs SlowLead front) can only ever grow in Ego's favor if Ego
  were to somehow go faster than 25.0 m/s (it cannot - its own cruise
  target is fixed at 20.0 m/s), so this author's ORIGINAL prediction was
  that cleared_lead reads false for the entire run. MEASURED instead:
  cleared_lead reads false through the whole pass phase (as predicted) but
  flips true in the same frame the phase transitions to signal_back - see
  the MEASURED / FINDING note above and the companion .expectations.yaml
  for why that turned out to be a phase-coupled telemetry artifact rather
  than a contradiction of this prediction. Meanwhile SlowLead vacates the
  ORIGINAL lane -2 ahead of Ego, so by the time SIGNAL_BACK's dwell+gap-
  acceptance are evaluated, the return gap is open (nothing else occupies
  lane -2 anywhere near Ego) - confirmed by the measured 3.00s inbound
  indicator lead (dwell was never skipped).

  StopTrigger=60s: generous relative to the un-accelerated sibling's ~43.5s
  full-route time, to give the safety-valve-forced SIGNAL_BACK/BACK hops
  and settling time to complete and be observed.

  SlowLead / policies / Ego cruise-speed convention: identical to the other
  08_overtake scenarios - see overtake_slow_lead_on_two_lane_road.xosc's
  header comment. policies: [overtake, lead] only - lane_change_initiation
  is NOT enabled (design doc section 6: the safety valve's own call reads
  an internally-overridden enabled=true copy of lc_init_cfg_ regardless of
  the config flag).
-->
<OpenSCENARIO>
   <FileHeader revMajor="1"
               revMinor="1"
               date="2026-08-04T00:00:00"
               description="VirtualDriver verification: SlowLead accelerates past Ego's own cruise speed mid-pass, so Ego can never clear it - the only way PASS ever ends is the section 5-2 safety valve forcing the return hop"
               author="GT_esmini"/>
   <ParameterDeclarations>
      <ParameterDeclaration name="EgoCruiseSpeed" parameterType="double" value="20.0"/>
      <ParameterDeclaration name="SlowLeadInitialSpeed" parameterType="double" value="8.0"/>
      <ParameterDeclaration name="SlowLeadAcceleratedSpeed" parameterType="double" value="25.0"/>
   </ParameterDeclarations>
   <CatalogLocations/>
   <RoadNetwork>
      <LogicFile filepath="../../../scenario_authoring/road_catalog/generated/straight_restricted_exit__l800_lanes2_exitm2.xodr"/>
   </RoadNetwork>
   <Entities>
      <ScenarioObject name="Ego">
         <Vehicle name="car_white" vehicleCategory="car" model3d="../../../models/car_white.osgb">
            <BoundingBox>
               <Center x="1.4" y="0.0" z="0.9"/>
               <Dimensions width="2.0" length="5.0" height="1.8"/>
            </BoundingBox>
            <Performance maxSpeed="69" maxDeceleration="30" maxAcceleration="10"/>
            <Axles>
               <FrontAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="2.98" positionZ="0.4"/>
               <RearAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="0" positionZ="0.4"/>
            </Axles>
            <Properties>
               <Property name="model_id" value="0"/>
               <Property name="scaleMode" value="ModelToBB"/>
            </Properties>
         </Vehicle>
         <ObjectController>
            <Controller name="VirtualDriverController">
               <Properties>
                  <Property name="esminiController" value="VirtualDriverController"/>
               </Properties>
            </Controller>
         </ObjectController>
      </ScenarioObject>
      <ScenarioObject name="SlowLead">
         <Vehicle name="car_yellow" vehicleCategory="car" model3d="../../../models/car_yellow.osgb">
            <BoundingBox>
               <Center x="1.4" y="0.0" z="0.9"/>
               <Dimensions width="2.0" length="5.0" height="1.8"/>
            </BoundingBox>
            <Performance maxSpeed="69" maxDeceleration="30" maxAcceleration="10"/>
            <Axles>
               <FrontAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="2.98" positionZ="0.4"/>
               <RearAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="0" positionZ="0.4"/>
            </Axles>
            <Properties>
               <Property name="model_id" value="1"/>
               <Property name="scaleMode" value="ModelToBB"/>
            </Properties>
         </Vehicle>
      </ScenarioObject>
   </Entities>
   <Storyboard>
      <Init>
         <Actions>
            <Private entityRef="Ego">
               <PrivateAction>
                  <TeleportAction>
                     <Position>
                        <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-2" offset="0" s="30"/>
                     </Position>
                  </TeleportAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <RoutingAction>
                     <AssignRouteAction>
                        <Route name="ego_route" closed="false">
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-2" offset="0" s="30"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                           <!--
                             Explicit connecting-road Waypoint (junction 100,
                             connection id=2, connecting road 101) - same
                             requirement as the other 08_overtake scenarios.
                           -->
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="101" laneId="-1" offset="0" s="30.1"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                           <Waypoint routeStrategy="shortest">
                              <Position>
                                 <LanePosition roadId="2" laneId="-1" offset="0" s="40"/>
                              </Position>
                           </Waypoint>
                        </Route>
                     </AssignRouteAction>
                  </RoutingAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <LongitudinalAction>
                     <!--
                       Init-side SpeedAction. REQUIRED, and not redundant with the
                       Story-side one below. ControllerVirtualDriver::ResolveTargetSpeed()
                       only picks up a LONG_SPEED action while it is RUNNING; a
                       dynamicsShape="step" action can complete before the controller ever
                       observes it, leaving last_action_target_ pinned at its seed value
                       (object_->GetSpeed() at the first Step). Measured 2026-08-04 without
                       this action: ego.speed stayed 0.0 and ego.s stayed 30.000444 for the
                       whole run. Setting the speed here makes that seed the cruise speed,
                       so the ego is at v_pass from t=0 and the distance budget in this
                       file's header holds exactly (no acceleration ramp to subtract).
                     -->
                     <SpeedAction>
                        <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                        <SpeedActionTarget>
                           <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$EgoCruiseSpeed"/>
                        </SpeedActionTarget>
                     </SpeedAction>
                  </LongitudinalAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <ControllerAction>
                     <ActivateControllerAction lateral="true" longitudinal="true"/>
                  </ControllerAction>
               </PrivateAction>
            </Private>
            <Private entityRef="SlowLead">
               <PrivateAction>
                  <TeleportAction>
                     <Position>
                        <LanePosition roadId="0" laneId="-2" offset="0" s="75"/>
                     </Position>
                  </TeleportAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <LongitudinalAction>
                     <SpeedAction>
                        <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                        <SpeedActionTarget>
                           <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$SlowLeadInitialSpeed"/>
                        </SpeedActionTarget>
                     </SpeedAction>
                  </LongitudinalAction>
               </PrivateAction>
            </Private>
         </Actions>
      </Init>
      <Story name="OvertakeStory">
         <Act name="OvertakeAct">
            <ManeuverGroup maximumExecutionCount="1" name="EgoSequence">
               <Actors selectTriggeringEntities="false">
                  <EntityRef entityRef="Ego"/>
               </Actors>
               <Maneuver name="CruiseManeuver">
                  <Event name="Cruise" priority="overwrite">
                     <Action name="CruiseAction">
                        <PrivateAction>
                           <LongitudinalAction>
                              <SpeedAction>
                                 <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                                 <SpeedActionTarget>
                                    <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$EgoCruiseSpeed"/>
                                 </SpeedActionTarget>
                              </SpeedAction>
                           </LongitudinalAction>
                        </PrivateAction>
                     </Action>
                     <StartTrigger>
                        <ConditionGroup>
                           <Condition name="CruiseStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                              <ByValueCondition>
                                 <SimulationTimeCondition value="0.0" rule="greaterThan"/>
                              </ByValueCondition>
                           </Condition>
                        </ConditionGroup>
                     </StartTrigger>
                  </Event>
               </Maneuver>
            </ManeuverGroup>
            <StartTrigger>
               <ConditionGroup>
                  <Condition name="ActStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                     <ByValueCondition>
                        <SimulationTimeCondition value="0" rule="greaterThan"/>
                     </ByValueCondition>
                  </Condition>
               </ConditionGroup>
            </StartTrigger>
         </Act>
         <Act name="SlowLeadAccelerateAct">
            <ManeuverGroup maximumExecutionCount="1" name="SlowLeadSequence">
               <Actors selectTriggeringEntities="false">
                  <EntityRef entityRef="SlowLead"/>
               </Actors>
               <Maneuver name="AccelerateManeuver">
                  <!--
                    THE ABORT-INDUCING EVENT: fires once, at t=8.0s -
                    comfortably after Ego enters PASS (the sibling
                    overtake_slow_lead_on_two_lane_road scenario, same
                    g0=40 setup, measured pass@6.40s) - and steps SlowLead
                    from 8.0 to 25.0 m/s, i.e. FASTER than Ego's own 20.0
                    m/s cruise. Ego can never clear a lead that is now
                    permanently pulling away, so PASS can only ever end via
                    the section 5-2 safety valve.
                  -->
                  <Event name="Accelerate" priority="overwrite">
                     <Action name="AccelerateAction">
                        <PrivateAction>
                           <LongitudinalAction>
                              <SpeedAction>
                                 <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0.0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                                 <SpeedActionTarget>
                                    <AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$SlowLeadAcceleratedSpeed"/>
                                 </SpeedActionTarget>
                              </SpeedAction>
                           </LongitudinalAction>
                        </PrivateAction>
                     </Action>
                     <StartTrigger>
                        <ConditionGroup>
                           <Condition name="AccelerateStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                              <ByValueCondition>
                                 <SimulationTimeCondition value="8.0" rule="greaterThan"/>
                              </ByValueCondition>
                           </Condition>
                        </ConditionGroup>
                     </StartTrigger>
                  </Event>
               </Maneuver>
            </ManeuverGroup>
            <StartTrigger>
               <ConditionGroup>
                  <Condition name="SlowLeadActStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                     <ByValueCondition>
                        <SimulationTimeCondition value="0" rule="greaterThan"/>
                     </ByValueCondition>
                  </Condition>
               </ConditionGroup>
            </StartTrigger>
         </Act>
      </Story>
      <StopTrigger>
         <ConditionGroup>
            <Condition name="StopCondition" delay="0" conditionEdge="rising">
               <ByValueCondition>
                  <SimulationTimeCondition value="60" rule="greaterThan"/>
               </ByValueCondition>
            </Condition>
         </ConditionGroup>
      </StopTrigger>
   </Storyboard>
</OpenSCENARIO>
